;; R2-carriers.edn -- the declared carriers of node R2 (PERCEIVE, "Structured
;; observation"), for worklist row :V7 slice 2.
;;
;; WHAT A "CARRIER" IS HERE, and it is not what it was for R5. R5's carriers
;; (sim/R5-carriers.edn) are a state space, a policy family, a belief and a C:
;; the arguments an equation needs. R2's registry row carries no equation --
;; aif-equations.edn:76 states a BOUNDARY, "o_t <- structured observation of the
;; world after action u_{t-1}" -- so what R2 declares about itself is not a
;; formula but a SHAPE: fourteen named channels, each with a source path, a
;; projection and a range. This file transcribes that shape from its declaration
;; sites, and the harness (v7_r2_node_sim.clj) checks the shipped node against
;; it.
;;
;; INDEPENDENCE, STATED EXACTLY. :reference below is transcribed from the
;; DECLARATION -- the channel table (observation.clj:18-32), the requirement
;; paths (observation.clj:49-65) and the docstrings -- and is evaluated by a
;; generic interpreter in the harness. It is not a copy of observe's body: the
;; body is a literal fourteen-key map (observation.clj:121-145) and this is a
;; table. What that buys is real but bounded: it catches an arithmetic or
;; source-path error in observe, and it does NOT catch an error shared by the
;; declaration and the body, because both were written by the same hand. Every
;; claim about the DECLARED RANGE is therefore checked separately, by probe, and
;; against the shipped producer -- not by reference agreement.
;;
;; :producer names the code that actually supplies the channel's source field in
;; a live scan, and :producer-range is a CODE-READING claim about that code, with
;; the file:line that carries it. It is not a measurement. The measurement of the
;; range is the trace-corpus leg of the harness, over the 889 observation vectors
;; the shipped node has already written.
;;
;; NOT A RULING. Nothing here is written to aif-equations.edn :choices or to
;; control-map-edges.edn :decisions.
{:id :R2-carriers-v1
 :node :R2
 :for "worklist.edn :V7 slice 2 (2026-09-06)"
 :registry-row "aif-equations.edn:74-79 -- the single :observe row, :class :stack-defined"

 :declaration-sites
 {:channel-table "src/futon2/aif/observation.clj:11-32 (observation-channels, the ordered vector)"
  :requirement-paths "src/futon2/aif/observation.clj:48-65 (channel-statuses' requirements map)"
  :absence-envelope "src/futon2/aif/observation.clj:66-76 (the {:variant :absent :reason :source-field-missing :coerced-to 0.0} record)"
  :projection "src/futon2/aif/observation.clj:103-146 (observe)"
  :vector-boundary "src/futon2/aif/observation.clj:148-158 (sense->vector, which refuses a non-matching envelope)"
  :range-assertion ["src/futon2/aif/observation.clj:5-7 (namespace docstring: 'a 14-channel observation vector in [0,1]')"
                    "src/futon2/aif/observation.clj:18-32 (every channel line carries [0,1] or an equivalent)"
                    "src/futon2/aif/observation.clj:104-105 (observe's docstring: 'channel-id -> [0,1] value')"]
  :call-site "scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:5936 (obs/observe scan-data), route-tagged :R2 at scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:5937"
  :scan-data-assembly "scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:7066-7086"}

 ;; :reference is the spec the harness interprets. Kinds:
 ;;   :path         value = (get-in data path default)
 ;;   :ratio        value = num/den when den is present and positive, else default
 ;;   :capped-scale value = min(cap, num/scale), num defaulting to 0
 ;;   :capped-pair-density  den = n(n-1)/2 from :n; value = min(cap, num/den) when den > 0, else default
 ;;   :capped-count-ratio   den = (count (get-in data den-path [])); value = num/den when den > 0, else default
